#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [equality, traits, enum]
# doc: |
#   D46's ENUM row, in the QUALIFIED-VARIANT-CONSTRUCTOR spelling
#   (`Direction.North() == Direction.North()`) — the exact shape `todo/t0013`
#   was filed about, and the one the Book's own chapter 6 demonstrated. It is
#   worth its own seed because the spelling parses as a METHOD CALL on the
#   identifier `Direction`, not as a call, so a lane that resolves equality
#   operands only through call/identifier inference silently misses it and
#   accepts. Unit variants are not exempt: before D46 the comparison answered
#   ADDRESS IDENTITY here too, so two distinct `North()` objects compared
#   unequal — it was never even a tag comparison.
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_UnsupportedOperator
#!end

enum Direction:
    North()
    South()

void main():
    if Direction.North() == Direction.North():
        print("equal")
    else:
        print("NOT-equal")
